                <pb facs="0210" n="198" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg198"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.00/1790: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Mr. William Phillips, Personal
                        Representative of President Roosevelt in India</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-02-20T17:00:00-04:00">February 20,
                            1943—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>108. Such comment as has been observed in American press regarding Gandhi’s fast
                    and situation arising therefrom has for the most part been factual and
                    unemotional. Implications involved are probably not appreciated by American
                    public and it is thought that there has been thus far little reaction to
                    existing situation. Censorship in India has undoubtedly greatly restricted
                    possible coverage here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
